    {
      "bbox": [
        173,
        1427,
        1489,
        2055
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "§ 4. Procedural Requisites. Subject to the following limitations, The Agency Chief Contracting Officers (\"ACCO\") of the Department of Health and the Department of Environmental Protection (\"DEP\") may exercise the function of certifying pursuant to section 327 of the Charter that the procedural requisites for the solicitation and award of contracts have been met, provided that the Director has made a determination in writing that each agency possesses the capacity to comply with procedural requirements, and such determination is concurred in by the Deputy Mayor for Operations; provided also, that an appropriate post-audit protocol has been agreed to by the agency and the Director. The ACCO of DEP shall exercise this certification function only in connection with engineering and architectural services contracts. All other DEP consulting or other contracts shall remain subject to certification by the Director. The Director shall periodically review each ACCO's performance of the function of certifying that procedural requisites have been met, and if such performance is found unsatisfactory, the Director shall revoke the ACCO's authority to",
